 "notes": "HAYSTAC quantum-enhanced (squeezed-state) haloscope search. Headline: 90% CL exclusion of axions with g_gamma >= 1.38 x g_gamma^KSVZ over the combined 16.96-17.12 and 17.14-17.28 ueV/c^2 windows (4.100-4.140 and 4.145-4.178 GHz; the 4.140-4.145 GHz TE mode is skipped, giving the gap near 17.12-17.14 ueV). Curve = frequency-resolved solid blue 90%-exclusion line in Fig.3a (|g_gamma/g_gamma^KSVZ| vs nu_a), extracted by pixel tracking from the raster figure (figs/excl_2020.JPEG); linear y-axis calibrated on ticks 0.5-2.0, x-axis 4.10 GHz + 0.01 GHz/tick. Rolling-median smoothed over pixel noise, decimated to 60 pts. Conversions: m_a[eV]=h*nu=4.135667e-6*nu[GHz]; g_agamma=|g_gamma/g_gamma^KSVZ|*g_KSVZ with g_KSVZ=alpha*|g_gamma^KSVZ|/(pi*f_a), g_gamma^KSVZ=-0.97, alpha=1/137.036, f_a[GeV]=5.7e6/m_a[eV] (QCD relation m_a=5.7ueV*1e12GeV/f_a). At m=17ueV, 1.38xKSVZ -> g_agamma=9.3e-15 GeV^-1. DM density not stated explicitly in this paper; HAYSTAC standard rho=0.45 GeV/cm^3 assumed (limit assumes axions saturate local halo). Reported per compilation convention (paper-native density, no rescaling).",
